{"title":"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In an arcade game, the \"monster\" is the shaded sector of a circle of radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> cm, as shown in the figure. The missing piece (the mouth) has central angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/0/f90d2feb8621ba116b5f134a36c633e11c5cf098.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\usepackage{gensymb} 60\\degree$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" />. What is the perimeter of the monster in cm?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/4/644027ee6d7418a42a6ab23a334ce3978943a716.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(100); defaultpen(linewidth(0.7)); filldraw(Arc(origin,1,30,330)--dir(330)--origin--dir(30)--cycle, yellow, black); label(&quot;1&quot;, (sqrt(3)/4, 1/4), NW); label(&quot;$60^\\circ$&quot;, (1,0));[/asy]\" width=\"168\" height=\"152\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/5/1058b3fea8b3e141b3ce1aa7be1d1474157fea33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A)\\ } \\pi+2 \\qquad \\mathrm{(B) \\ }2\\pi \\qquad \\mathrm{(C) \\  } \\frac{5}{3}\\pi \\qquad \\mathrm{(D) \\  } \\frac{5}{6}\\pi+2 \\qquad \\mathrm{(E) \\  }\\frac{5}{3}\\pi+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"496\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The two straight sides of the \"monster\" are radii of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> cm, so their total length is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/b/39b50ce24de2036ae4e7cab78aa48b503ab588e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+1 = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" /> cm. The circular arc forms <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/b/6aba98bddeb686d47e924a382c933c618732f3e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{360^{\\circ}-60^{\\circ}}{360^{\\circ}} = \\frac{5}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"126\" height=\"39\" /> of the entire circle, and a circle with radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> cm has circumference <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/e/93e6dd64a8a9a1eb6d0fc099afffbc93c00cfaf9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\pi(1) = 2\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"90\" height=\"20\" /> cm, so the length of the arc is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/3/42312288422e0ef9dded9cc492842d31adda4c81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{5}{6}\\right)(2\\pi) = \\frac{5}{3}\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"127\" height=\"45\" /> cm. Hence the total perimeter in cm is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/2/3f21672ab54c20bbf50aa4c20bcee651bea2f426.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{(E)} \\ \\frac{5}{3}\\pi+2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"98\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME\" title=\"1985 AHSME\">1985 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1985 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1985\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 6